Quality constraints

Keep the solution small, generic and deterministic.

There must be one universal implementation, not duplicated logic across Battle, Watch Mode and Practice Ground.

Do not put the mechanic in rendering or UI code.

Do not create fighter-specific configuration for it.

Do not use browser timers.

Do not round simulation timestamps based on wall time.

Avoid magic numbers when the Launch system can own named constants.

Respect the repository’s module responsibility rules and source-scanning architecture tests.

Before finishing, inspect the diff for stale comments or documentation that still says Launch Point only increases.

Acceptance criteria

The change is complete when a fighter who takes a hit gets the usual Launch Point increase and launch calculation, stays at that value for a full 2 seconds without another real hit, then loses exactly 1 Launch Point every 0.5 seconds until reaching 0; any later real hit adds its damage and completely restarts that timing; Shielded/blocked hits do not restart it; no value can fall below 0; this behaves identically for every fighter and every shared hit source; respawns/restarts remain clean; Discover/spec/system documentation explains the new mechanic; and the full node --test suite passes.

When done, provide a concise implementation summary, list the files changed, describe the timing/state model you chose, and report the test commands and results.
